<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Civil war</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Civil war, armed conflict between rival factions within a single state, is a recurring cause of imperial decline. Succession disputes, regional rebellions and rivalry among generals drained resources, divided armies and invited foreign intervention. Examples include the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>'s civil wars, the fitnas that divided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun</a> and Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a>, the dynastic wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo Empire</a>'s civil wars after 1665.</p></div>
